      "text": "We can simplify the equation by multiplying both sides by $x+2$:\n\\[5(x+2) = x^3 - 2x^2 - 8x.\\]\nExpanding and rearranging, we get:\n\\[x^3 - 2x^2 - 12x - 10 = 0.\\]\nWe can factor this equation as:\n\\[(x+1)(x-2)(x-5) = 0.\\]\nSo the solutions are $x = -1, 2,$ and $5$.\nThe sum of the $x$-values that satisfy the equation is $-1 + 2 + 5 = \\boxed{6}$.\nThe answer is: 6",
